{"id": "EUVD-2026-81996", "enisaUuid": "21ab82e2-6c71-37eb-80f4-be7f86da9c32", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ntty: skip cdev_del() when no cdev is registered\n\nTTY device registration can fail before a cdev is allocated.\nSerial core keeps the port so setserial can still use it, and later\nremoval passes the NULL cdev slot to cdev_del(), causing a NULL-pointer\ndereference.\n\nOnly delete the cdev when the slot is not NULL.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:08:48", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:51:04", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ea3d2fae7c1d6492145976553817d22e8ef69a0e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/21031bd0d662549412378110c989b164feb6e4be", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2af4c46b429907edc8cb069c78fca1d950120b98", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3dbf85ef40b6366ba15e882f7536cdc98bea579a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c3b5623fd97648f2747444aa8932ae604662df93"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-90335", "GHSA-5wc4-c9q8-2q27"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "36c44aef-bd6b-3e3b-8d1f-45d305d606d7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a3a10ce3429e5dee623ad5c8407ea58e204fcb0a <21031bd0d662549412378110c989b164feb6e4be"}, {"id": "3bf1bc6e-77fa-330f-90b4-03ac6602ef4f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.57"}, {"id": "69c761ca-10c1-34da-b9e9-db91167a9729", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.3"}, {"id": "740f652c-1c05-3f0a-8669-23f5980ac7af", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "8937fdfb-7ccd-3c39-aae2-e3ce70af8e93", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a3a10ce3429e5dee623ad5c8407ea58e204fcb0a <2af4c46b429907edc8cb069c78fca1d950120b98"}, {"id": "90c6b121-1fd2-3dd9-9f77-7883ca8277d0", "product": {"name": "Linux"